.TH NOCTURNE 1 "2026-08-19" "nocturne 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
nocturne \- an apartment building in your terminal that flashes with your music
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nocturne
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Draws a night-time apartment building whose windows flash on musical onsets:
bass hits light big scattered bursts, mids medium ones, hi-hats single
sparkles. By default it taps the Mac's system audio through the bundled
.B nocturne-tap
helper (Core Audio process taps, macOS 14.4+), so it visualizes whatever is
playing \- Music.app, Cider, a browser. The first run triggers the System
Audio Recording permission prompt.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-app \fIname\fR
Tap a single app's audio (e.g. \-\-app Music) instead of the system mix.
.TP
.B \-\-file \fIpath\fR
Play an audio file through afplay and visualize it.
.TP
.B \-\-web
Also serve the web version on localhost and open it in the browser,
live-mirrored to the same audio stream.
.TP
.B \-\-port \fIn\fR
Port for \-\-web (default 4173).
.TP
.B \-\-sim
Fake 120bpm onsets instead of tapping audio. Demo and testing.
.TP
.B \-\-seed \fIn\fR
Building seed; the same seed gives the same building.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help.
.SH STATUS LINE
When tapping live audio, nocturne shows the playing track in the status line
(and in the web mirror): it asks Music.app via osascript (without launching
it), then Cider's local API on port 10767 if a token is set. No token, no
Cider label; the visualizer itself is unaffected.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NOCTURNE_TAP
Path to the nocturne-tap helper binary, overriding PATH lookup.
.TP
.B NOCTURNE_CIDER_TOKEN
Cider External Application API token (Cider: Settings > Connectivity) for the
track label.
.B JUKEBOX_CIDER_TOKEN
is honored as a fallback.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B q
Quit.
.TP
.B r
New building (reseed).
.SH FILES
.TP
.B nocturne-tap
Audio tap helper, installed next to nocturne in ~/.bun/bin. Emits FFT frames
as JSON lines; nocturne finds it via PATH or $NOCTURNE_TAP.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR afplay (1)
